  "question": {
    "text": "An octahedral complex having molecular composition Co. $5 \\mathrm{NH}_3. \\mathrm{Cl}. \\mathrm{SO}_4$ has two isomers A and B. The solution of A gives a white precipitate with $\\mathrm{AgNO}_3$ solution and the solution of B gives white precipitate with $\\mathrm{BaCl}_2$ solution. The type of isomerism exhibited by the complex is,",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "SFtTG",
      "text": "Co-ordinate isomerism",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "zpALG",
      "text": "Linkage isomerism",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "F3U5M",
      "text": "Ionisation isomerism",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "uVt9q",
      "text": "Geometrical isomerism",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "(A) complex is $\\left[\\mathrm{Co}\\left(\\mathrm{NH}_3\\right)_5\\left(\\mathrm{SO}_4\\right)\\right] \\mathrm{Cl}$<br />(B) complex is $\\left[\\mathrm{Co}\\left(\\mathrm{NH}_3\\right)_5 \\mathrm{Cl}\\right] \\mathrm{SO}_4$<br />Both $(\\mathrm{A})$ and $(\\mathrm{B})$ are Ionisation isomers.",
    "image": null
  },
